CLAUDE.md is down from 42,215 to 23,889 bytes, and a new test fails the build if it goes over 40,000 again. The full check suite passed and the work is committed as f94bd908.

What moved. 15 MCP history paragraphs went from CLAUDE.md's "MCP gotchas" section into ARCHITECTURE.md (the Day 180 #841 paragraphs, the Day 181 #842 and "third door" paragraphs, and the Day 240 note). So did the Day-192 history at the end of the BUILTIN_TOOL_NAMES paragraph. They sit under a new heading, "src/agent_builder.rs + src/mcp_prefix.rs — MCP history", with a note saying where they came from. A script checked that every removed line appears unchanged in ARCHITECTURE.md.

What CLAUDE.md keeps:
• the Day-39 explanation of why tool-name collisions kill a session;
• the paragraph on how colliding servers are connected under a prefix;
• a short summary of how things work now, with a pointer to the ARCHITECTURE.md entry;
• the BUILTIN_TOOL_NAMES sync rule and the four things that read that list.

A correction in the summary. My first draft of the summary was wrong about current behaviour, and I fixed it before committing. It said a failed connect is reported to the user through connections_lost_note. The code shows otherwise: an MCP failure prints a red ✗ mcp: line and the agent is kept. Only an OpenAPI failure rebuilds the agent and prints connections_lost_note.

The new test. this_repos_claude_md_stays_under_its_40kb_budget in tests/instruction_size.rs reads the repo's own CLAUDE.md and fails if it is over 40,000 bytes. The failure message gives the byte count, the rule ("New history goes in ARCHITECTURE.md") and the fix. It also checks the file is not empty and contains "## Safety Rules", so pointing it at the wrong file can't make it pass.

Comment fixes in `src/instruction_size.rs`. The 41_713 row and the threshold's doc comment (lines 12–14) both described this repo's own CLAUDE.md as the case that must not warn. Both now point to the new 40 KB gate. The doc comment was not on the task's list, but it made the same claim, so I changed it too.

Checks:
• Test proven to fail: I appended filler, ran the gate and watched it fail by name ("CLAUDE.md is 43889 bytes, over its 40000-byte budget"), then restored the file (confirmed identical with cmp) and it went green, 3/3. I used 20,000 bytes of filler instead of the 5,000 the plan said, because at 23.9 KB the smaller amount would not cross the limit.
• Full suite: cargo build, cargo test (35 test binaries passed), cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings, cargo fmt -- --check, and bash tests/harness_logic.sh (336 passed, 0 failed) all pass.
